efect rather than a limit: assertions.py declares the status shape as locality "local" | "remote" | "none" and check_local_by_default computes PASS if locality == "local" and active is True else FAIL, so a target honestly reporting "none" -- exactly this target's default configuration, embeddings.model "" at build/defaults/preferences/zotero.js:121, isEnabled() false at xpcom/embeddings.js:179-181 -- is scored fail against a clause reading "the embedder is local". It is not failing to be local. Driven red against a local fake with the "local" control beside it rather than argued; reported and NOT repaired, and this adapter never reaches that assertion anyway, its status being absent independently. (2) THE ROSTER'S MOST COMPLETE STATUS OBJECT HAS NO TRANSPORT: xpcom/embeddings.js:2872-2889 returns enabled, model, indexing, stopping, paused, phase, per-library indexed/eligible and indexedAttachments/eligibleAttachments, download and extraction progress and the last error -- a closer fit to this layer's normalized status and to SPEC.md 5.2.8's coverage sentence than anything else on the roster publishes -- and its own comment says it is "for the preferences UI". Enumerating every Zotero.Server.Endpoints registration under xpcom/server/ at this head reaches the connector, integration and local-API sets and none names Zotero.Embeddings or Zotero.ML, and the local API is 403 by default in any case. So status is absent for a fifth kind of reason: not missing, not behind an opt-in, but computed, complete and unreachable. (3) PAUSE AND RESUME MATCH THE RATIFIED DEFINITION ALMOST VERBATIM AND THE HARNESS CANNOT REACH THEM: stopIndexing at :3141-3150 clears both queues and persists embeddings.indexingPaused, isPaused at :1824-1826 reads it back, "persisted so a stop survives a restart" in the target's own comment, and startIndexing at :2965-2971 is documented safe to call while running and re-enqueues work skipped by source hash rather than rebuilt. Both are called from ONE place, preferences/preferences_advanced.js:103 and :107, a GUI pane -- and both would govern nothing while embeddings.model is "" (:1809 gates the work on isEnabled()). MEASURED, NOT READ, on padme 2026-09-03 against the built tree: every /api/ route answers 403 "Local API is not enabled" (httpServer.localAPI.enabled false at build/defaults/preferences/zotero.js:173, gated at xpcom/server/server_localAPI.js:249) on /api/, on /api/users/0/items with q= and with qmode=everything, on /api/users/0/settings and on POST /api/local/authorize; GET /connector/ping answers 200 "Zotero is running" and its POST form a fixed connector-preferences bundle naming nothing about retrieval; no embeddings.sqlite is created; and after a clean shutdown the profile carries 46 preference lines, not one of them under extensions.zotero.embeddings. or search.bestMatch, which is how the shipped defaults are shown to be the effective ones. That last figure corrects an earlier arm here that read ONE line: the count depends on how the process is stopped, a short stop measuring a different state rather than a cleaner one. The eight probes are committed at bench/results/0583-zotero-6012/http-surface.json, and they RESOLVE the code=000 the lane's build smoke left open -- the server does answer; a short smoke had not reached the point where it listens. R10, three cells over a 75 s dwell with the lane lead's own driver (bench/r10_host_baseline.py, PR #234) so the numbers are comparable: virgin-isolated 0 off-machine / 430 name lookups, warmed-isolated 0 / 60, and a net-shared control of 423 / 82 that trips both detectors. Beside Zotero 10.0.1 on the same machine and driver -- 0 / 426, 0 / 60, 456 / 80 -- THE PULL REQUEST ADDS NO MEASURABLE EGRESS, stated as an observation about two runs and never subtracted in code. The arena state is declared because it moves the figure sevenfold: this adapter runs virgin, the expensive end. R10's attribution wall arrives here in its purest form and inverts: the plugin