--- body ---
## Context

The ratified target-neutral harness names Zotero core PR #6012 as its
platform-native target. Ticket 0578 builds the assertion layer and first
adapter; this ticket adds #6012 without teaching the layer Zotero internals.
Its query surface is in-process or UI-facing rather than Zotero's local HTTP
API, which is the architectural difference this target exists to exercise.

## Actions

1. Pin the tested #6012 revision and make its build reproducible.
2. Declare derived state, query access, process lifecycle, default
   configuration and unsupported interface verbs per SPEC.md §5.2.8.
3. Implement only the minimal transport needed to exercise offered surfaces.
4. Run every applicable assertion and record not-offered distinctly for the
   rest, especially uninstall if Zotero core exposes no genuine equivalent.

## Exit criteria

- [x] pinned #6012 revision and reproducible target setup
- [x] adapter passes the declaration-only contract checks from ticket 0578
- [x] every interface verb yields pass, fail, not-offered or not-run
- [x] no assertion layer code names #6012 or its internal file layout
- [x] `make check` and `erg check tickets/` pass
